yDream Shaders is built on the MakeUp UltraFast codebase by Javier Garduño
(https://github.com/javiergcim/MakeUpUltraFast), distributed under the
GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0. The base architecture, and the
lower-level techniques credited below, come from that project.

yDream Shaders extends that base with its own sky, stars, constellation,
cloud, water, atmosphere, lighting, shadow and color systems, plus the
Distant Horizons and Northstar integrations listed below.

------

SKY AND STAR DATA

- Star positions and magnitudes are derived from the HYG Database v4.1
  by David Nash (AstroNexus).
  Source: https://github.com/astronexus/HYG-Database
  License: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
  (CC BY-SA 4.0) — https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
  Modifications: the catalog was filtered to the 500 brightest stars
  (apparent magnitude <= 4), and Right Ascension / Declination were
  converted to 3D direction vectors for GPU rendering. The resulting
  arrays (hero_stars.glsl) are considered a derivative work of the HYG
  catalog and are shared under CC BY-SA 4.0, in addition to the LGPL
  v3.0 that covers the rest of the pack.

- Constellation line geometry is derived from d3-celestial by Olaf Frohn.
  Source: https://github.com/ofrohn/d3-celestial
  License: BSD-3-Clause. Copyright (c) 2015-2024, Olaf Frohn.
  The full license text is reproduced in LICENSE.txt.
  Modifications: filtered to the 20 most famous constellations, and each
  endpoint was converted from (RA, Dec) to a 3D unit vector.

- The underlying constellation figures follow the IAU 88-constellation
  standard.
  Reference: https://www.iau.org/public/themes/constellations/

------

ANTI-ALIASING

- TAA is based on Erkaman's TAA simple implementation:
  https://gist.github.com/Erkaman
  The current implementation has been substantially rewritten to add
  YCoCg variance clipping, Catmull-Rom history sampling, age-based
  blending and jittered reprojection, but the original conceptual
  starting point is Erkaman's gist.

- Conceptual references for temporal supersampling and reprojection:
  Brian Karis, "High Quality Temporal Supersampling", SIGGRAPH 2014.
  Lasse Jon Fuglsang Pedersen, "Temporal Reprojection Anti-Aliasing in
  INSIDE", GDC 2016.

- SMAA (Subpixel Morphological Antialiasing) is based on the reference
  implementation by Jorge Jimenez, Jose I. Echevarria, Belen Masia,
  Fernando Navarro and Diego Gutierrez.
  Source: https://github.com/iryoku/smaa
  License: MIT. The full license text is reproduced in LICENSE.txt.

------

CLOUDS

- The volumetric cloud raymarch, erosion, and multi-scatter lighting
  are conceptually based on:
  Andrew Schneider & Nathan Vos, "The Real-Time Volumetric Cloudscapes
  of Horizon: Zero Dawn", SIGGRAPH 2015.
  Sebastien Hillaire, "Physically Based Sky, Atmosphere & Cloud
  Rendering in Frostbite", SIGGRAPH 2016.

- Cloud-noise hashing and field sampling are original to yDream, with
  the two-octave rotation trick adapted from in-house work.

------

HASHING AND NOISE

- The `cheapHash3` helper used for per-night constellation selection is
  based on the "Hash without Sine" algorithm by Dave Hoskins.
  Source: https://www.shadertoy.com/view/4djSRW
  License: MIT. Copyright (c) 2014 David Hoskins.

- Phi noise by delu:
  https://www.shadertoy.com/view/Nst3R7
  Based on TinyTexel:
  https://www.shadertoy.com/view/wltSDn
  Based on:
  http://extremelearning.com.au/unreasonable-effectiveness-of-quasirandom-sequences/

- R dither based on:
  http://extremelearning.com.au/unreasonable-effectiveness-of-quasirandom-sequences/

- Dither 13 and Dither 17 by atyuwen:
  https://www.shadertoy.com/view/wl3cWX
  Based on:
  https://developer.oculus.com/blog/tech-note-shader-snippets-for-efficient-2d-dithering/

- Interleaved noise from:
  "NEXT GENERATION POST PROCESSING IN CALL OF DUTY: ADVANCED WARFARE"
  http://advances.realtimerendering.com/s2014/index.html

------

LIGHTING AND SHADOWS

- Enhanced ambient occlusion is based on Capt Tatsu's ambient occlusion
  used in BSL Shaders:
  https://bitslablab.com/bslshaders/

- Shadow bias technique from Emin implementation, based on a concept
  reimagined by gri573:
  https://www.complementary.dev/

- Screen-space sun occlusion for Distant Horizons LOD terrain and for
  vanilla terrain beyond the shadow map range, the unified trace, and
  the four-way occlusion toggle system were implemented specifically
  for yDream.

